# Sanity. All three are NEXT_PUBLIC_, so they are compiled into the
# client bundle and are not secrets — the real values are kept here so a
# fresh clone builds with `cp .env.example .env.local`. Access is
# controlled by dataset visibility and API tokens, never by hiding these.
#
# Set the same three in Vercel (Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables) before deploying: sanity/env.ts throws at import time if
# any is missing, so the build fails loudly rather than querying the
# wrong dataset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=4eid4gr5
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_API_VERSION=2026-01-01
